{"title":"2013 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ann, Bill and Cathy went bowling. In bowling, each score is a whole number.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After three games, Cathy’s average score was 113. She scored the same in her fifth game as she did in her fourth game. Is it possible for her average score on these five games to be 120? Explain why or why not.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since Cathy's average score was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a13c73adb40f8ff5e6c628d59394386477a683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$113$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games, her total score for the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40cec99e4a750590087d3ebb0fa3e55ce821ca90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$113 \\times 3 = 339$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>If Cathy were to get an average score of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games, her total score for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> games would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed8e454412585f09a7ede7fefd6188990ba19b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 \\times 5 = 600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, the total for the last two games would have to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/5656552ef26fb8047a61ddc31e134010aecee912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$600 - 339 = 261$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>However, since she scored the same in her fifth and fourth game and there's two games, the total would have to be even because the score in each game must be a whole number. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe6399d0b3d150415301c84bb7103d2de951507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$261$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> even, so it is not possible for Cathy's average score on the five games to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232501\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 43/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 153/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1940/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.540      1 2013_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.540      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36971:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232501 and revision id 285869. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}